वशि, इस्, m. subjugation, fascination, bewitching,
holding others in magical submission to the will;
(इ), n. the state of being subject, subjection.

वाशी, f., Ved. roaring, crying, singing; a weapon
of the Maruts, an axe, spear, weapon in general;
(according to some, perhaps) the roaring thunder-
bolt, (according to Sāy. = आराख्यम् आयुधम्);
voice, speech (= वाच्, Naigh.

] he is called the son of the Apsaras
Urvaśī by Mitra and Varuṇa, whence his patronymic
Maitrāvaruṇi; in Manu

